// 소스를 연 채로 인용을 적는다. w1 의 quote 는 notes/body.txt 의 한 줄이거나, 표처럼 여러 줄에 걸친 것은 줄을 이어 붙인 텍스트(브라우저 textContent 와 같다)다. 차트 점은 notes/figures.md 의 aria-label 이다. 모든 quote 가 해당 파일에 글자 그대로 있는지 스크립트로 확인했다.
{"id":"e1","source":"w1","locator":"§intro ¶1","quote":"Introducing Claude Sonnet 5.5, the second model in the Claude 5.5 family. It’s a clear upgrade over Claude Sonnet 5, runs 30%+ faster, and costs up to 30% less for most work.","why":"글 전체의 주장: 30%+ 빠르고 대부분 일에서 최대 30% 저렴"}
{"id":"e2","source":"w1","locator":"§intro ¶2","quote":"Where Opus 5.5 is built for complex work requiring careful judgment, Sonnet 5.5 is strongest at well-scoped everyday tasks, fixing bugs, and creating polished documents, slides, and spreadsheets.","why":"Opus 5.5 와의 역할 분담"}
{"id":"e3","source":"w1","locator":"§intro · Performance","quote":"Sonnet 5.5 scores 70.6% on Terminal-Bench 4.0, an agentic coding evaluation, compared to Sonnet 5’s 10.3%. It scores two points below Opus 5.5 on GDPval-AA, a test of real-world work across a variety of occupations.","why":"Terminal-Bench 70.6% 대 10.3%, GDPval 2점 차"}
{"id":"e4","source":"w1","locator":"§intro · Cost","quote":"Sonnet 5.5 is priced the same as Sonnet 5 at $2 per million input tokens, $10 per million output tokens, and $0.20 per million tokens for cache reads, but it typically needs far fewer tokens to do the same work. In our testing, it costs up to 30% less per task than its predecessor.","why":"가격 동일, 절감은 토큰 수에서만 온다"}
{"id":"e5","source":"w1","locator":"§intro · Speed","quote":"Sonnet 5.5 generates outputs 30%+ faster than Sonnet 5, making it our fastest Sonnet model to date.","why":"속도 30%+"}
{"id":"e6","source":"w1","locator":"§intro · Alignment and safety","quote":"Because its cybersecurity capabilities are comparable to Opus 5’s, it’s the first Sonnet model to launch with cyber safeguards and fallbacks like those we’ve developed for our most capable models. Its biology safeguards are the same as Sonnet 5’s.","why":"Sonnet 최초의 cyber 안전장치, bio 는 Sonnet 5 와 같음"}
{"id":"e7","source":"w1","locator":"§Performance ¶1","quote":"On several evaluations, Sonnet 5.5 at Max effort even performs comparably to Opus 5.5. However, benchmark scores capture only one facet of a model’s capabilities; in our own testing, and in that of external testers, Opus 5.5 remains clearly stronger at complex, open-ended work requiring sustained judgment.","why":"원문의 자기 할인"}
{"id":"e8","source":"w1","locator":"§Performance · table","quote":"Agentic codingTerminal-Bench 4.070.6%10.3%66.4%¹—","why":"표 TB4: Sonnet 5.5 / Sonnet 5 / Opus 5.5 / GPT-6 Sol"}
{"id":"e9","source":"w1","locator":"§Performance · table","quote":"Agentic codingFrontierCode 1.1 (Main)46.2%Max²42.4%54.4%49.3%52.1%Xhigh","why":"표 FC: max 46.2%, xhigh 52.1% 병기"}
{"id":"e10","source":"w1","locator":"§Performance · table","quote":"Agentic codingCursorBench 4.055.5%34.1%57.8%—","why":"표 CB"}
{"id":"e11","source":"w1","locator":"§Performance · table","quote":"Knowledge workGDPval-AA v2.1³1844144918461487⁴","why":"표 GDPval (⁴ 는 각주 표시)"}
{"id":"e12","source":"w1","locator":"§Performance · table","quote":"Knowledge workAA-Briefcase v1.1³1811135918221483⁴","why":"표 AA-Briefcase (⁴ 는 각주 표시)"}
{"id":"e13","source":"w1","locator":"§Performance · table","quote":"Multidisciplinary reasoningHumanity’s Last Exam64.5%with tools54.9%with tools67.7%with tools—","why":"표 HLE"}
{"id":"e14","source":"w1","locator":"§Performance · table","quote":"Computer useOSWorld 2.180.1%partial57.0%partial81.8%partial—","why":"표 OSWorld 2.1"}
{"id":"e15","source":"w1","locator":"§Performance · table","quote":"Visual chart recognitionChartography61.6%no tools15.6%no tools64.4%no tools53.6%⁴no tools","why":"표 Chartography"}
{"id":"e16","source":"w1","locator":"§Performance · charts ¶","quote":"On several benchmarks, Sonnet 5.5 at Low or Medium effort beats Sonnet 5’s best score for about a tenth of the cost per task. It complements Opus 5.5 best when running at lower effort settings, where it costs less per task. At higher settings, it can perform comparably at a similar cost.","why":"낮은 effort 에서 1/10 비용, 높은 effort 에서는 Opus 5.5 와 비슷한 비용"}
{"id":"e17","source":"w1","locator":"§Performance · Terminal-Bench caption","quote":"At Medium effort, the default in the Claude apps, Sonnet 5.5 far exceeds Sonnet 5’s best score for less than a tenth of the cost per task.","why":"TB 캡션, 앱 기본 Medium"}
{"id":"e18","source":"w1","locator":"§Performance · FrontierCode caption","quote":"At High effort, the default on the Claude Platform, Sonnet 5.5 matches GPT-6 Sol’s best score for about a fifth of the cost per task.²","why":"FC 캡션, Platform 기본 High"}
{"id":"e19","source":"w1","locator":"§Performance · CursorBench caption","quote":"Sonnet 5.5 at Low effort exceeds Sonnet 5’s best score for less than a tenth of the cost per task.","why":"CB 캡션"}
{"id":"e20","source":"w1","locator":"§Performance · AA-Briefcase caption","quote":"On AA-Briefcase, a new benchmark of long-horizon knowledge work, Sonnet 5.5 at Medium effort bests Sonnet 5’s best score for about one ninth of the cost per task.³","why":"Briefcase 캡션"}
{"id":"e21","source":"w1","locator":"§Coding ¶1","quote":"At High effort on FrontierCode, it scores 10 points higher than Sonnet 5 at the same setting, at about one fifteenth of the cost per task. On CursorBench, which tests models on tasks from real Cursor coding sessions, its best score is within about two points of Opus 5.5.","why":"FC high 끼리 10점, 1/15 비용"}
{"id":"e22","source":"w1","locator":"§Coding ¶2","quote":"They were also struck by its efficiency: in head-to-head runs, it batched tool calls together more than Sonnet 5, leading to fewer steps and lower costs.","why":"tool call 묶음"}
{"id":"e23","source":"w1","locator":"§Coding · Epic Games","quote":"The new model managed tens of thousands of lines of code for gameplay system architecture, kept responses snappy, handled multi-hour tasks, and delivered with less prescriptive prompting.","why":"고객 인용"}
{"id":"e24","source":"w1","locator":"§Coding · Every","quote":"Fast at coding and can be steered quickly in iterative workflows. But it can still work long if it needs to.","why":"고객 인용"}
{"id":"e25","source":"w1","locator":"§Coding · CodeRabbit","quote":"Sonnet 5’s tendency to reach for web search too often and its high token use are both gone in this new model. We plan to move simple and moderate reviews over now, and more in the coming weeks.","why":"고객 인용, 이전 범위"}
{"id":"e26","source":"w1","locator":"§Coding · SpaceXAI","quote":"Claude Sonnet 5.5 delivers frontier-level performance on CursorBench 4.0 at 55.5%, second only to Opus 5.5.","why":"고객 인용"}
{"id":"e27","source":"w1","locator":"§Coding · Base44","quote":"Across 118 real app builds, Claude Sonnet 5.5 produced apps that scored level with Opus 5. It got there in 3.6 iterations per build on average, where Opus 5 took 7.7. It had the fewest failed tool calls of any model we compared.","why":"고객 인용 수치"}
{"id":"e28","source":"w1","locator":"§Coding · Unity","quote":"The majority of Claude Sonnet 5.5’s work passed that check. It also completed 90% of tasks in our multi-step Unity Editor and coding benchmark, beating similar models.","why":"고객 인용 수치"}
{"id":"e29","source":"w1","locator":"§Coding · Creator","quote":"When Claude Opus 5.5 sets the architecture and general framework for a game, I would feel confident in letting Sonnet 5.5 implement it.","why":"Opus 설계, Sonnet 구현 분담"}
{"id":"e30","source":"w1","locator":"§Knowledge work ¶1","quote":"On GDPval-AA, which tests models on real-world tasks across 44 occupations and nine major industries, Sonnet 5.5 scores nearly level with Opus 5.5 and about 400 points above Sonnet 5.","why":"GDPval 약 400점"}
{"id":"e31","source":"w1","locator":"§Knowledge work ¶2","quote":"In one internal test, we gave it a public company’s quarterly earnings materials and call transcripts, along with a slide template, and asked for a 10-slide operating review. Two experts judged its first draft to be ready to send as is.","why":"내부 시험"}
{"id":"e32","source":"w1","locator":"§Knowledge work · Slack","quote":"Without changing any of our prompts, Claude Sonnet 5.5 did better than Sonnet 5 on almost all of our offline Slackbot evals, in fewer steps and with about 14% fewer output tokens.","why":"고객 인용, 프롬프트 그대로"}
{"id":"e33","source":"w1","locator":"§Knowledge work · Zendesk","quote":"It made fewer wrong decisions and resolved tickets faster than the Claude models we use in production today. Tickets were processed 20% faster","why":"고객 인용 수치"}
{"id":"e34","source":"w1","locator":"§Knowledge work · Balyasny","quote":"On our private suite of 2,441 finance tasks covering Q&A, extraction, analysis, and forecasting, Claude Sonnet 5.5 scored ahead of Sonnet 5 and used about 121k tokens per answer, where Sonnet 5 used 497k.","why":"고객 인용 토큰"}
{"id":"e35","source":"w1","locator":"§Knowledge work · Box","quote":"Compared to the last model, Sonnet 5.5 was more accurate, 2.4x faster, and used 12% fewer total tokens.","why":"고객 인용"}
{"id":"e36","source":"w1","locator":"§Knowledge work · Lovable","quote":"Our coding evals showed a third fewer tool calls and roughly half the shell runs to finish a task.","why":"고객 인용"}
{"id":"e37","source":"w1","locator":"§Knowledge work · Atlassian","quote":"Claude Sonnet 5.5 will allow teams to run their Rovo Agents up to 30% faster than they could with Sonnet 5.","why":"고객 인용"}
{"id":"e38","source":"w1","locator":"§Cost and speed · pricing table","quote":"Cache reads$0.20$0.20Cache writes$2.50$5Input tokens$2$4Output tokens$10$20","why":"Sonnet 5.5 / Opus 5.5 가격표"}
{"id":"e39","source":"w1","locator":"§Cost and speed ¶2","quote":"In Claude Code and our apps, the default effort is set to Medium, while the Claude Platform defaults to High.","why":"제품별 기본 effort"}
{"id":"e40","source":"w1","locator":"§Safety · Alignment ¶1","quote":"Sonnet 5.5 doesn’t advance the frontier of our models’ capabilities, so our alignment assessment focused on a targeted set of risks that apply to models of any capability level","why":"평가 범위를 좁힌 이유"}
{"id":"e41","source":"w1","locator":"§Safety · Alignment ¶2","quote":"On our automated behavioral audit, which tests Claude across roughly 1,850 scenarios, Sonnet 5.5 improves on or matches Sonnet 5 on most measures of alignment, resistance to misuse, and honesty.","why":"행동 감사 1,850 시나리오"}
{"id":"e42","source":"w1","locator":"§Safety · Safeguards · Cybersecurity","quote":"Users can still find and fix bugs in their code as part of routine software development, but higher-risk cybersecurity tasks will visibly fall back to Sonnet 5.","why":"cyber fallback 은 Sonnet 5"}
{"id":"e43","source":"w1","locator":"§Safety · Safeguards · Biology","quote":"These target harmful requests; most research, education, and clinical work is unaffected, though some microbiology and virology requests may be flagged in error.","why":"bio 오탐 인정"}
{"id":"e44","source":"w1","locator":"§Safety · Safeguards · Distillation","quote":"it’s the first Sonnet model to launch with safety classifiers that prevent reasoning extraction. Sonnet 5.5 also expands preserved thinking, so Claude’s thinking cannot be decoupled from the account that created it. Most developers won’t notice a change. If you move conversations between accounts, including switching accounts mid-session in Claude Code, our docs article explains the change.","why":"reasoning extraction 분류기, 계정 결속"}
{"id":"e45","source":"w1","locator":"§Getting started","quote":"If you run Sonnet with thinking off, you’ll need to switch to the new between_tools setting, which keeps up-front thinking off, before moving to Sonnet 5.5.","why":"소개 글이 직접 적은 유일한 코드 변경"}
{"id":"e46","source":"w1","locator":"§Footnotes 2","quote":"Sonnet 5.5 scores lower at Max effort than at Xhigh. FrontierCode evaluates whether a code change could be merged without human edits. It penalizes out-of-scope changes, even if they are high-quality or helpful. At Max effort, Sonnet 5.5 more often ran Claude Code’s code-review skill, which splits the review across many subagents, and in two cases Cognition examined, this led to a timeout or to extra edits beyond the task’s scope, and therefore to a lower score.","why":"max 가 xhigh 보다 낮은 이유"}
{"id":"e47","source":"w1","locator":"§Footnotes 3","quote":"Artificial Analysis ran GDPval-AA and AA-Briefcase on a pre-release deployment of Sonnet 5.5 on the Claude Platform, which we found to have a bug that could degrade responses to requests that use structured outputs.","why":"structured outputs 버그"}
{"id":"e48","source":"w1","locator":"chart Terminal-Bench 4.0","quote":"Sonnet 5.5 · Low: 20.0% $0.76 / Sonnet 5.5 · Med: 28.8% $0.83 / Sonnet 5.5 · High: 43.0% $1.94 / Sonnet 5.5 · Xhigh: 61.5% $5.30 / Sonnet 5.5 · Max: 70.6% $12.54","why":"TB effort 곡선"}
{"id":"e49","source":"w1","locator":"chart Terminal-Bench 4.0","quote":"Sonnet 5 · High: 4.5% $8.20 / Sonnet 5 · Max: 10.3% $11.62","why":"Sonnet 5 비교점"}
{"id":"e50","source":"w1","locator":"chart FrontierCode v1.1 main","quote":"Sonnet 5.5 · Low: 29.3% $0.19 / Sonnet 5.5 · Med: 36.5% $0.24 / Sonnet 5.5 · High: 49.4% $0.42 / Sonnet 5.5 · Xhigh: 52.1% $1.59 / Sonnet 5.5 · Max: 46.2% $20.78","why":"FC effort 곡선, max 가 가장 비싸고 낮다"}
{"id":"e51","source":"w1","locator":"chart FrontierCode v1.1 main","quote":"Sonnet 5 · High: 39.4% $6.10 / Sonnet 5 · Xhigh: 42.7% $10.07 / Sonnet 5 · Max: 42.4% $17.12 / GPT-6 Sol · Max: 49.3% $2.07","why":"FC 비교점"}
{"id":"e52","source":"w1","locator":"chart CursorBench 4.0","quote":"Sonnet 5.5 · Low: 35.8% $0.50 / Sonnet 5.5 · Med: 39.2% $0.70 / Sonnet 5.5 · High: 47.8% $1.67 / Sonnet 5.5 · Xhigh: 53.1% $3.88 / Sonnet 5.5 · Max: 55.5% $9.67","why":"CB effort 곡선"}
{"id":"e53","source":"w1","locator":"chart CursorBench 4.0","quote":"Sonnet 5 · High: 30.8% $3.48 / Sonnet 5 · Max: 34.1% $7.17","why":"CB 비교점"}
{"id":"e54","source":"w1","locator":"chart AA-Briefcase v1.1","quote":"Sonnet 5.5 · Low: 1264.0 $0.87 / Sonnet 5.5 · Med: 1461.0 $1.64 / Sonnet 5.5 · High: 1634.0 $3.95 / Sonnet 5.5 · Xhigh: 1746.0 $9.63 / Sonnet 5.5 · Max: 1811.0 $29.19","why":"Briefcase effort 곡선"}
{"id":"e55","source":"w1","locator":"chart AA-Briefcase v1.1","quote":"Sonnet 5 · High: 1177.0 $3.76 / Sonnet 5 · Max: 1359.0 $14.43 / Opus 5.5 · Max: 1822.0 $21.05","why":"Briefcase 비교점"}
{"id":"e56","source":"d1","locator":"§Send a request","quote":"It leaves out five settings that return a 400 error:","why":"400 을 내는 설정 다섯"}
{"id":"e57","source":"d1","locator":"§Thinking runs by default · table","quote":"| Claude Sonnet 5.5                      | On                                  | `\"adaptive\"`, `\"between_tools\"`                      | `\"omitted\"`       |","why":"Sonnet 5.5 thinking.type 허용값"}
{"id":"e58","source":"d1","locator":"§Thinking runs by default · table","quote":"| Claude Sonnet 5                        | On                                  | `\"adaptive\"`, `\"disabled\"`                           | `\"omitted\"`       |","why":"Sonnet 5 는 disabled 허용"}
{"id":"e59","source":"d1","locator":"§Turn off up-front thinking ¶1","quote":"To turn off up-front thinking on Claude Sonnet 5.5, send `thinking: {\"type\": \"between_tools\"}`. It's the lowest thinking setting. Its progress updates between tool calls still come back as `thinking` blocks with their summary text. Without tools, the response contains only text.","why":"between_tools 의 동작"}
{"id":"e60","source":"d1","locator":"§Turn off up-front thinking ¶1","quote":"On Claude Sonnet 5.5, `disabled` returns a 400 `invalid_request_error`:","why":"disabled 400"}
{"id":"e61","source":"d1","locator":"§Turn off up-front thinking ¶2","quote":"`between_tools` works on every platform that offers Claude Sonnet 5.5, with no beta header. It's accepted at `low`, `medium`, and `high` effort. At `xhigh` or `max`, it returns a 400 error.","why":"between_tools 는 high 이하만"}
{"id":"e62","source":"d1","locator":"§Turn off up-front thinking ¶2","quote":"`between_tools` takes no other field: `display`, `budget_tokens`, or `block_binding` sent with it returns a 400 error. With [server-side fallback](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/refusals-and-fallback#server-side-fallback), a `between_tools` request that falls back to Claude Sonnet 5 runs there with `thinking: {\"type\": \"disabled\"}`.","why":"between_tools 추가 필드 400, fallback 시 disabled"}
{"id":"e63","source":"d1","locator":"§Turn off up-front thinking ¶3","quote":"With `between_tools`, effort can't change mid-conversation: a per-message `output_config.effort` that differs from the level in effect returns a 400 error.","why":"between_tools 에서 effort 고정"}
{"id":"e64","source":"d1","locator":"§Forced tool use","quote":"Every earlier model on this page accepts a `tool_choice` of type `any` or `tool`. Claude Sonnet 5.5 rejects both with a 400 error, including on the [token counting](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/token-counting) endpoint:","why":"forced tool_choice 400"}
{"id":"e65","source":"d1","locator":"§Forced tool use ¶2","quote":"Send `tool_choice: {\"type\": \"auto\"}`, and mark the tool `strict: true` so its input matches the schema. The model can then answer without calling the tool, so say in the prompt when to use it.","why":"대체: auto + strict"}
{"id":"e66","source":"d1","locator":"§Forced tool use ¶2","quote":"On Amazon Bedrock, [structured outputs](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/structured-outputs), which include strict tool use, aren't available for Claude Sonnet 5.5. There, send `auto` without `strict`, say in the prompt when to call the tool, and validate the tool input in your code.","why":"Bedrock 예외"}
{"id":"e67","source":"d1","locator":"§Forced tool use ¶3","quote":"A request can have at most 20 strict tools, and the MCP, computer use, and browser use toolset entries don't accept `strict`.","why":"strict 20개 한도"}
{"id":"e68","source":"d1","locator":"§Thinking blocks are tied ¶1","quote":"Claude Sonnet 5.5 reads thinking blocks from Claude Sonnet 5, Claude Opus 4.8, Claude Haiku 4.5, and earlier models. It doesn't read blocks from Claude Opus 5, Claude Opus 5.5, or any Claude Fable or Claude Mythos model. The API drops blocks the model can't read. The request still returns 200, and dropped blocks aren't billed.","why":"모델 검사 방향"}
{"id":"e69","source":"d1","locator":"§Thinking blocks are tied ¶2","quote":"For accounts created on or after August 31, 2026, 00:00 UTC, the API enforces this by default, on the Claude API, Amazon Bedrock, and Google Cloud. On those accounts, a request that replays a block after an edit to earlier history returns a 400 error.","why":"prefix 검사 적용 계정"}
{"id":"e70","source":"d1","locator":"§Thinking blocks are tied ¶2","quote":"Thinking blocks that Claude Sonnet 5.5 produces work only in the account that produced them, or in an account linked to it.","why":"계정 결속"}
{"id":"e71","source":"d1","locator":"§Computer use","quote":"On the Claude API and Google Cloud, Claude Sonnet 5.5 supports computer use only through the `computer_toolset_20260801` toolset. There, `computer_20251124` returns a 400 error. Claude Sonnet 5.5 doesn't accept `computer_20250124` on any platform.","why":"computer use 400"}
{"id":"e72","source":"d1","locator":"§Computer use ¶2","quote":"If you send the `fine-grained-tool-streaming-2025-05-14` beta header, remove it when you move to the toolset. Alongside a toolset entry, it returns a 400 error. Set `eager_input_streaming: true` on each tool that needs it instead.","why":"beta header 400"}
{"id":"e73","source":"d1","locator":"§Advisor tool","quote":"With the [advisor tool](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/advisor-tool), a Claude Sonnet 5.5 executor needs one of these advisors: Claude Opus 5, Claude Opus 5.5, Claude Sonnet 5.5, Claude Fable 5, Claude Fable 5.1, Claude Mythos 5, or Claude Mythos 5.1. Claude Opus 4.8, Claude Opus 4.7, Claude Opus 4.6, Claude Sonnet 5, and Claude Sonnet 4.6 advisors return a 400 error. The advice comes back encrypted as an `advisor_redacted_result` block, so its text isn't readable in the response.","why":"advisor 짝"}
{"id":"e74","source":"d1","locator":"§Text between tool calls ¶1","quote":"On Claude Sonnet 5.5, notes longer than a sentence or two that the model writes between tool calls come back as [progress-update `thinking` blocks](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/thinking#progress-updates), empty at the default `display`. Shorter remarks stay `text`.","why":"tool call 사이 텍스트"}
{"id":"e75","source":"d1","locator":"§Text between tool calls ¶2","quote":"With adaptive thinking, set `display` to `\"updates\"` (beta, `thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18` header) to get the updates alone, or to `\"summarized\"` to get them mixed with reasoning. Render each non-empty `thinking` block before the `tool_use` block that follows it. With [`between_tools`](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/models/sonnet-5-5/migration-guide#turn-off-up-front-thinking), the text comes back without `display`.","why":"display 설정"}
{"id":"e76","source":"d1","locator":"§Safety classifiers and fallback","quote":"Claude Sonnet 5.5 declines in more categories than Claude Sonnet 5. A decline returns `stop_reason: \"refusal\"`, and its `stop_details` can name one of these [categories](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/refusals-and-fallback#refusal-response):","why":"거부 부류"}
{"id":"e77","source":"d1","locator":"§Safety classifiers and fallback","quote":"* **`\"general_harms\"`:** The request falls under another usage-policy area. Benign work can also trigger this category.","why":"general_harms 오탐"}
{"id":"e78","source":"d1","locator":"§Safety classifiers and fallback ¶2","quote":"[Server-side fallback](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/refusals-and-fallback#server-side-fallback) (`fallbacks: \"default\"`, beta, Claude API only) retries `\"cyber\"` and `\"frontier_llm\"` declines on Claude Sonnet 5. It doesn't retry `\"bio\"`, `\"reasoning_extraction\"`, or `\"general_harms\"` declines.","why":"fallback 재시도 범위"}
{"id":"e79","source":"d1","locator":"§Other changes","quote":"* **Prompt caching:** The minimum cacheable prompt is 512 tokens, down from 1,024 on Claude Sonnet 5, Claude Sonnet 4.6, and Claude Sonnet 4.5.","why":"캐시 최소 512"}
{"id":"e80","source":"d1","locator":"§Recommended changes","quote":"Re-run your effort sweep. Claude Sonnet 5.5 has five effort levels: `low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh`, and `max`. The default on the Claude API is `high`. The levels are recalibrated, so a level doesn't produce the same amount of thinking as on Claude Sonnet 5.","why":"effort 재조정"}
{"id":"e81","source":"d1","locator":"§Recommended changes","quote":"Start at `high` unless your workload is agentic or latency-sensitive. For agentic coding and multistep tool use, start at `medium` for well-specified tasks and move to `high` for harder or longer ones. For chat and other latency-sensitive work, start at `medium` or `low`.","why":"권장 시작 effort"}
{"id":"e82","source":"d1","locator":"§Migration checklist · Every starting model","quote":"* [Re-run your effort sweep](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/models/sonnet-5-5/migration-guide#recommended-changes), and re-baseline cost.","why":"체크리스트 마지막 항목"}
{"id":"e83","source":"d1","locator":"§Migrating from Sonnet 5 ¶1","quote":"Replace your model ID with `claude-sonnet-5-5`, which has no date suffix.","why":"모델 ID"}
{"id":"e84","source":"d1","locator":"§Handle thinking in responses","quote":"* **Revisit `max_tokens`.** It covers thinking plus text, and thinking tokens are billed as output tokens.","why":"max_tokens"}
{"id":"e85","source":"d1","locator":"§intro note","quote":"If you use [Claude Managed Agents](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/managed-agents/overview), no changes beyond updating the model name are required.","why":"Managed Agents 예외"}
{"id":"e86","source":"d2","locator":"§Effort levels · table","quote":"| `high` (default on most models)       | Claude thinks on most requests that benefit from it. Provides deep reasoning on complex tasks.   |","why":"high 는 대부분 모델의 기본"}
{"id":"e87","source":"d2","locator":"§Effort levels · table","quote":"| `medium` (default on Claude Opus 5.5) | Claude uses moderate thinking. May skip thinking for simple queries.                             |","why":"medium 기본은 Opus 5.5 뿐"}
{"id":"e88","source":"d2","locator":"§Effort levels ¶2","quote":"At every level, Claude decides per request whether to think. In a tool-use loop, the first request after new user input typically carries most of the reasoning, and follow-up requests that only process tool results can skip thinking, including at `xhigh` and `max`.","why":"adaptive 의 뜻"}
{"id":"e89","source":"d2","locator":"§Prompt caching","quote":"The resolved effort value is rendered into the prompt, so changing it between requests invalidates cache breakpoints, just as changing the legacy [`budget_tokens`](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/extended-thinking#extended-thinking-with-prompt-caching) parameter does on models that use it. Setting `effort` explicitly to the model's default is equivalent to omitting it and does not break the cache.","why":"effort 변경은 캐시를 깬다"}
{"id":"e90","source":"d2","locator":"§Cost control","quote":"At `high` effort and above, Claude may think extensively and is more likely to exhaust the budget.","why":"max_tokens 소진"}
{"id":"e91","source":"d2","locator":"§Pricing","quote":"What you're billed for is the same regardless of the `display` setting; only what you see changes:","why":"display 와 과금 무관"}
{"id":"e92","source":"d2","locator":"§Pricing ¶3","quote":"To see how many billed output tokens were spent on internal reasoning, read `usage.output_tokens_details.thinking_tokens` in the response.","why":"thinking 토큰 관측"}
{"id":"e93","source":"w1","locator":"chart FrontierCode v1.1 main","quote":"Opus 5.5 · Low: 47.3% $0.40 / Opus 5.5 · Med: 54.6% $0.80 / Opus 5.5 · High: 54.0% $1.09 / Opus 5.5 · Xhigh: 51.4% $2.25 / Opus 5.5 · Max: 54.4% $6.19","why":"FC 의 Opus 5.5 점, medium 이 최고점"}
{"id":"e94","source":"w1","locator":"chart FrontierCode v1.1 main","quote":"Sonnet 5 · Low: 28.7% $2.39 / Sonnet 5 · Med: 35.2% $3.81 / GPT-6 Sol · Low: 37.3% $0.43 / GPT-6 Sol · Med: 45.9% $0.77 / GPT-6 Sol · High: 47.7% $1.04 / GPT-6 Sol · Xhigh: 48.4% $1.32","why":"FC 나머지 점"}
{"id":"e95","source":"w1","locator":"chart Terminal-Bench 4.0","quote":"Opus 5.5 · Xhigh: 66.4% $7.35 / Opus 5.5 · Max: 64.8% $11.24 / Sonnet 5 · Low: 3.2% $3.78 / Sonnet 5 · Med: 4.4% $4.83 / Sonnet 5 · Xhigh: 7.0% $9.95 / GPT-5.6 Sol · Low: 7.9% $1.46 / GPT-5.6 Sol · Max: 37.3% $7.89","why":"TB 비교점, Sonnet 5 는 모든 effort 에서 Sol 아래"}
{"id":"e96","source":"w1","locator":"chart CursorBench 4.0","quote":"Sonnet 5 · Low: 24.1% $1.39 / Sonnet 5 · Med: 28.0% $2.31 / Sonnet 5 · Xhigh: 32.0% $4.55 / Opus 5.5 · Max: 57.8% $13.43","why":"CB 나머지 점"}
{"id":"e97","source":"w1","locator":"chart AA-Briefcase v1.1","quote":"Sonnet 5 · Low: 923.0 $0.82 / Sonnet 5 · Med: 1056.0 $1.73 / Sonnet 5 · Xhigh: 1274.0 $7.56","why":"Briefcase 나머지 점"}
{"id":"e98","source":"d1","locator":"§Safety classifiers and fallback ¶3","quote":"Real-time cyber safeguards are new for code from Claude Sonnet 4.6, Claude Sonnet 4.5, and Claude Haiku 4.5. For legitimate security work, apply to the [Cyber Verification Program](https://support.claude.com/en/articles/14604842-real-time-cyber-safeguards-on-claude-opus-and-sonnet).","why":"4.6 이하에는 cyber 안전장치가 처음"}
{"id":"e99","source":"d1","locator":"§intro tip","quote":"The skill applies the model ID swap and, as needed, breaking parameter changes, prefill replacement, and effort calibration for your target model across your code base, then produces a checklist of items to verify manually.","why":"/claude-api migrate"}
{"id":"e100","source":"d1","locator":"§Other changes from Sonnet 4.6","quote":"* **About 30% more tokens:** Claude Sonnet 5.5 uses Claude Sonnet 5's tokenizer. Against Claude Sonnet 4.6, Claude Sonnet 4.5, and Claude Haiku 4.5, the same text produces about 30% more tokens, depending on the content.","why":"4.6 이하 토큰 30%"}
{"id":"e101","source":"d1","locator":"§Sonnet 4.6 breaking changes","quote":"**Sampling parameters return an error.** Claude Sonnet 4.6 and earlier models and Claude Haiku 4.5 accept `temperature`, `top_p`, and `top_k`. On Claude Sonnet 5.5, a non-default value returns a 400 error.","why":"4.6 이하 sampling 400"}
{"id":"e102","source":"d1","locator":"§intro ¶2","quote":"Claude Sonnet 5.5 has the same prices as Claude Sonnet 5.","why":"가격 동일 (guide)"}
{"id":"e103","source":"d2","locator":"§Cost control","quote":"If you see [`stop_reason: \"max_tokens\"`](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/thinking-troubleshooting#stopped-at-max-tokens) in responses, you have two remedies:","why":"max_tokens 처방"}
{"id":"e104","source":"d1","locator":"§Turn off up-front thinking · After example","quote":"      thinking={\"type\": \"between_tools\"},\n      output_config={\"effort\": \"high\"},","why":"guide 의 After 예시는 xhigh 를 high 로 내린다"}
{"id":"e105","source":"d1","locator":"§Turn off up-front thinking · Before example","quote":"      thinking={\"type\": \"disabled\"},\n      output_config={\"effort\": \"xhigh\"},","why":"Before 예시는 disabled 에 xhigh"}
{"id":"e106","source":"d3","locator":"§Recommended effort levels for Claude Sonnet 5","quote":"Claude Sonnet 5 defaults to `high` effort on the Claude API and Claude Code.","why":"Sonnet 5 기본 effort"}
{"id":"e107","source":"d3","locator":"§Recommended effort levels for Claude Sonnet 5.5","quote":"Claude Sonnet 5.5 also supports [changing effort mid-conversation](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/effort#change-effort-mid-conversation-beta) with a per-message `output_config`, which preserves the prompt cache.","why":"per-message effort 는 캐시 유지"}
{"id":"e108","source":"d3","locator":"§Per-message effort (beta)","quote":"Per-message effort is in beta and requires the [beta header](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/api/beta-headers) `mid-conversation-output-config-2026-07-01`.","why":"beta header"}
{"id":"e109","source":"d4","locator":"§Thinking blocks are tied","quote":"To drop the affected blocks instead, send the `thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01` beta header and set `thinking.block_binding.prefix_mismatch_behavior` to `\"drop_block\"`. On older accounts, setting that field to either value opts the request in. `block_binding` works only with `thinking: {\"type\": \"adaptive\"}`. With `between_tools`, keep the history append-only, or strip the thinking blocks from the edited turn on.","why":"이전 계정과 drop_block"}
{"id":"e110","source":"d4","locator":"§computer_20251124 is not supported","quote":"Drop the beta header, replace the `tools` entry with `{\"type\": \"computer_toolset_20260801\"}`, and update your agent loop for member `tool_use` blocks, batch actions, and `toolset_name` on results.","why":"agent loop 변경"}
{"id":"e111","source":"d4","locator":"§Feature support","quote":"Per-message effort, mid-conversation system messages, and mid-conversation tool changes aren't available on Claude Sonnet 5, whose minimum cacheable prompt is 1,024 tokens.","why":"Sonnet 5 에 없던 기능"}
{"id":"e112","source":"w1","locator":"§Performance · Terminal-Bench chart note","quote":"Terminal-Bench and OpenAI did not report GPT-6 Sol performance publicly, so we report GPT-5.6 Sol here.","why":"GPT-5.6 Sol 대체 이유"}
{"id":"e113","source":"w1","locator":"§Safety · Alignment ¶3","quote":"As we described in our recent alignment assessment, no set of evaluations reliably catches every failure","why":"평가의 한계"}
{"id":"e114","source":"w1","locator":"§Footnotes 4","quote":"Artificial Analysis does not expect major impacts to AA-Briefcase v1.1 and GDPval-AA v2.1. Internal testing of Chartography suggests its score was not impacted.","why":"각주 4 완화 문장"}
{"id":"e115","source":"d1","locator":"§Handle thinking in responses","quote":"Code that ran without thinking needs all three items. Code from Claude Sonnet 5 likely has the first two.","why":"Sonnet 5 코드는 대개 갖춤"}
{"id":"e116","source":"w1","locator":"§Footnotes 3","quote":"We expect the effect on Sonnet 5.5’s scores, if any, to be small and to understate its performance.","why":"if any"}
{"id":"e117","source":"d4","locator":"§Thinking blocks are tied ¶1","quote":"No other model reads Claude Sonnet 5.5 thinking blocks.","why":"반대 방향"}
{"id":"e118","source":"w1","locator":"§Safety · Safeguards · Cybersecurity","quote":"Sonnet 5.5’s cyber capabilities are a large improvement over Sonnet 5’s, so we’re deploying it with safeguards similar to those on Opus 5.5.","why":"안전장치는 Opus 5.5 와 비슷"}
{"id":"e119","source":"d3","locator":"§Recommended effort levels for Claude Sonnet 5.5","quote":"Use `xhigh` or `max` only where your evals show a quality gain. Set `max_tokens` with room for thinking and the reply.","why":"xhigh/max 는 eval 이 이득을 보일 때만"}
{"id":"e120","source":"d3","locator":"§Recommended effort levels for Claude Sonnet 5.5","quote":"For agentic coding, set `max_tokens` to 128,000, the model's maximum, and [stream](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/streaming) the response.","why":"agentic coding max_tokens 128,000"}
{"id":"e121","source":"d4","locator":"§Thinking blocks are tied","quote":"The API also checks whether anything before a Claude Sonnet 5.5 thinking block has changed since the block was produced: the `system` prompt, the `tools`, or an earlier message.","why":"prefix 검사 대상 셋"}
{"id":"e122","source":"d4","locator":"§Refusals, fallback, and billing","quote":"A declined request returns HTTP 200 with `stop_reason: \"refusal\"` and a [`stop_details`](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/refusals-and-fallback#refusal-response) object naming the policy area.","why":"거부는 200 으로 온다"}
{"id":"e123","source":"d1","locator":"§Text between tool calls ¶1","quote":"On Claude Sonnet 5 and earlier models, all text between tool calls comes back as `text` blocks. No request fails, but an interface that shows those notes goes quiet.","why":"조용한 변화"}
{"id":"e124","source":"d1","locator":"§Computer use ¶3","quote":"Code that already sends the toolset needs no change. [Migrate from `computer_20251124`](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/computer-use-tool#migrate-from-computer-20251124) lists the request and agent-loop changes.","why":"이미 toolset 이면 변경 없음"}
{"id":"e125","source":"d1","locator":"§Forced tool use ¶2","quote":"[Strict tool use](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/strict-tool-use) supports a subset of JSON Schema and needs `additionalProperties: false` on every object.","why":"strict 의 스키마 조건"}
{"id":"e126","source":"d4","locator":"§Forced tool use is not supported","quote":"`tool_choice: {\"type\": \"auto\"}` (the default) and `{\"type\": \"none\"}` are supported. The same check applies to the [token counting](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/token-counting) endpoint.","why":"auto 와 none 은 허용"}
{"id":"e127","source":"d4","locator":"§Thinking blocks are tied","quote":"So a conversation that moves from Claude Sonnet 5 onto Claude Sonnet 5.5 keeps its reasoning, and one that moves from Claude Sonnet 5.5 to any other model runs the turns after the switch without it.","why":"모델 전환 방향"}
{"id":"e128","source":"d2","locator":"§Cost control","quote":"In a tool-use loop, each request in the turn has its own `max_tokens`, so it doesn't bound the whole turn's spend.","why":"max_tokens 는 요청 단위"}
{"id":"e129","source":"d3","locator":"§Change effort mid-conversation","quote":"On Claude Fable 5.1, Claude Mythos 5.1, Claude Opus 5.5, Claude Opus 5, and Claude Sonnet 5.5, use a per-message effort change, which keeps the prompt cache. On other models, set a new top-level value on the next request, which starts the cache over.","why":"per-message effort 는 캐시 유지, Sonnet 5 는 새로 시작"}
{"id":"e130","source":"d4","locator":"§Turn off up-front thinking with between_tools","quote":"Pass those blocks back unchanged with the rest of the assistant turn. A progress-update block you send back gives the model the full note it wrote, not the summary.","why":"between_tools 의 블록도 되돌려 보낸다"}
{"id":"e131","source":"d4","locator":"§Thinking blocks stay with the account that produced them","quote":"When another account sends one of these blocks, the API drops the block before the model sees it, and the request succeeds.","why":"다른 계정의 블록은 빠지고 200"}
{"id":"e132","source":"d1","locator":"§Computer use · table","quote":"| `computer_20251124`    | Claude Sonnet 5, Claude Sonnet 4.6                   | `computer_toolset_20260801`             | `computer_20251124`    |","why":"Bedrock 에서는 computer_20251124 를 그대로"}
{"id":"e133","source":"d4","locator":"§computer_20251124 is not supported","quote":"Integrations that already use the toolset, and the [browser use tool](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/browser-use-tool), need no change.","why":"browser use tool 변경 없음"}
{"id":"e134","source":"d4","locator":"§Refusals, fallback, and billing","quote":"Whether a refusal that arrives before any output is billed depends on its refusal category, and it counts against your rate limits either way.","why":"거부 과금은 부류에 따라"}
{"id":"e135","source":"d1","locator":"§Turn off up-front thinking ¶2","quote":"To run at those levels, use adaptive thinking: omit the `thinking` field or send `thinking: {\"type\": \"adaptive\"}`.","why":"xhigh 를 지키려면 adaptive"}
{"id":"e136","source":"d1","locator":"§Turn off up-front thinking · error","quote":"\"thinking.type.disabled\" is not supported for this model. Use \"thinking.type.between_tools\" for the lowest thinking setting, or \"thinking.type.adaptive\" and \"output_config.effort\" to control thinking behavior.","why":"disabled 400 문구"}
{"id":"e137","source":"d1","locator":"§Forced tool use · After example","quote":"\"content\": \"What'\\''s the weather in Paris? Use the get_weather tool.\"","why":"After 예시는 프롬프트로 호출을 유도"}
{"id":"e138","source":"d4","locator":"§Availability","quote":"* **AWS:** [Claude in Amazon Bedrock](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/claude-in-amazon-bedrock), as `anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5`, and [Claude Platform on AWS](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/claude-platform-on-aws), as `claude-sonnet-5-5`.","why":"Bedrock 모델 ID"}
{"id":"e139","source":"d1","locator":"§Migrating from Sonnet 5 ¶1","quote":"On other platforms, use the ID listed under [Availability](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/models/sonnet-5-5/whats-new-sonnet-5-5#availability).","why":"플랫폼별 ID 는 Availability"}
{"id":"e140","source":"d4","locator":"§Some advisor tool pairings are not supported","quote":"With the [advisor tool](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/advisor-tool) (beta), a Claude Sonnet 5.5 executor needs Claude Mythos 5.1, Claude Fable 5.1, Claude Mythos 5, Claude Fable 5, Claude Opus 5.5, or Claude Opus 5 as its advisor, or Claude Sonnet 5.5 itself.","why":"advisor 는 beta"}
{"id":"e141","source":"d4","locator":"§Thinking blocks are tied","quote":"With the `thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01` beta header, the drop is reported in a top-level `input_transformations` array.","why":"빠진 블록은 beta header 로 보고된다"}
